# Large corpus/cache files -- essential to continue the pipeline, but too big for a
# normal git push (several are over GitHub's 100MB per-file limit; the whole cache/
# and most of data/ together are ~3.6GB). Transfer these separately -- see
# SESSION_HANDOFF.md's "Getting the data" section.
cache/
data/*.jsonl
data/*.xlsx

# Small, current review outputs -- keep these in git even though the *.xlsx rule
# above would otherwise exclude them.
!data/quantum_axis_case_review.xlsx
!data/cs_axis_case_review.xlsx

# Legacy/superseded data outputs from the archived phase1-3 and pillar-era scripts
# (scripts/unused_legacy/) -- small enough to fit, but not part of the current
# pipeline's output, so excluded for the same reason those scripts were archived.
data/*.csv
!data/quantum_axis_case_review.csv
!data/cs_axis_case_review.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store

# Stray scratch files from earlier sessions, not part of the current pipeline
pipeline_atlas.html
qb3_classifications.jsonl

# Jupyter checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
